  "id": "garbage-in-garbage-out",
  "term": "garbage in, garbage out",
  "definition": "\"Garbage in, garbage out\" means that the quality of a system’s results depends on the quality of the data put into it. In data-driven or machine-learning work, flawed, unrepresentative, or biased training data can produce flawed or biased outputs.",
